>Which brings up a YANI for one of the NetHack features that
>irritates me so much there's surely a patch for it already,
>but I'd like more.
>
>I play on a MS-Windows system and my game data files are
>identified by my user-id on that system (which happens to be
>Owner-Xanthian, but at least the Windows port of NetHack is
>smart enough to omit the "Owner-" part in greeting my PC
>during the game) .
>
>But that is really confounding two ideas: who owns the save
>file, for which that is the correct answer, versus what
>should be the name of the player character, which it seems
>more than a bit vain to have always named for me!
>
>I get around this by having several startup icons each of
>which sets the user name on the command line, (so I get
>file names prefixed "Owner-Dolan" or whatever, instead)  but
>this is also an ugly solution; creating one for each
>possible role/race/gender/alignment would exhaust my screen
>space.
>
>Modifying something each time I run NetHack is also an
>ugly solution; at the rate I burn through PCs, I'd spend
>half my time trying to think up new names.
>
>That stuff that should be set and forget, but out of the way
>and in as much detail as the user needs is exactly the sort
>of information that belongs in a startup file.
>

I have also thought about this several times, but I have not yet
implemented it as I think it would results in even more YASDs due to
role inexperience (i have never even tried a monk).In fact I played
Valkyries until I ascended,a Priest until I ascended, and more
recently a wizard (until I ascended recently).I will probably go back
to playing a Valkyrie as I still think i am inexperienced.

But I digress.
An easy way to implement separate names and alignment for each class
would be to write up a perl script to launch nethack, with a randomly
assigned class with separate defined (or even randomized per class)
names for each class.
e.g All Barbarians are called Conan and are chaotic.
All Wizards are either called Merlin (lawful),Belgarath
(neutral),Gandalf (lawful), Saruman (chaotic), or Radagast (neutral).
etc etc
This could all be bound up to call nethack defining name, class,
alignment etc via the command line. (it could even rewrite parts of
defaults.nh (or .nethackrc) instead for even more power)
Some refinement could be done to display currently saved games with
some kind of selection option (saved wizmode game OR saved Valkyrie
game OR saved healer game OR new randomized game OR predefined new
game).
It wouldnt be too difficult and it would be fairly patform
independent.
As I said before, I would write it up myself except I probably wouldnt
use it much. (All of my characters are called Gabkin and they are all
Valkyries at the moment...)
It isn't really all that difficult to do if you have moderate
programming/scripting skills.
I would be willing to collaborate with some one if they really wanted
to do it though... (user testing,feedback,coding/scripting help etc)

